{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"icecold-rusted-fowl","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\n\n`tests/_topology_template.py` cannot copy a store template when the source is a **linked worktree** whose `.tickets-tracker/.git` is a read-only `gitdir:` pointer file. The copy step raises:\n\n```\nPermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied:\n  'C:\\Users\\runneradmin\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\pytest-of-runneradmin\\pytest-1\\popen-gw0\\\n   test_half_fixed_copy_is_reject0\\half\\.tickets-tracker\\.git'\n```\n\nEvery test whose fixture builds a per-test store template then fails at setup. In the Windows advisory sweep (workflow `294845723`, run `35250748887`) this single defect accounts for **1361 of 3008 red outcomes — 45.2%**, as one fixture defect with 1361 dependents.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Run `35250748887` (2026-09-17 17:07Z, ref `4f12815e9a0b`): 1626 failed + 1382 errors = 3008 top-level red outcomes. Classified from the final unindented `short test summary info` block of `gh run view --log-failed`, excluding nested subprocess pytest summaries.\n- Run `35511654149` (2026-09-20 12:48Z): 1636 failed + 1383 errors = 3019 — the class persists.\n- Full six-way cause classification is recorded on `6798-606d`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`_rewrite_embedded_paths()` rewrites **every** copied metadata file with `path.write_bytes(rewritten)`.\n\nIn a linked worktree, `.git` is not a directory — it is a **file** containing `gitdir: <path>`. The copy preserves its mode, which is read-only. `write_bytes` therefore reopens a read-only file with `mode='wb'`.\n\nPOSIX permits that silently for the copying user. Windows refuses it with `PermissionError`. The code encodes a POSIX-only assumption: *a copied Git marker file can always be reopened in place for writing*.\n\nThis is the same underlying fact behind bug 84aa — a linked worktree's `.git` is a pointer, not a directory.\n\n## Planned change\n\nGuard the rewrite by **shape**, not by platform:\n\n- When a rewrite targets a `.git` file whose original bytes begin with `gitdir:`, temporarily add owner-write permission, write the rewritten pointer, then **restore the original mode**.\n- Every other path keeps its current behaviour unchanged.\n\nRestoring the mode matters: the read-only marker is part of what the copied store asserts, so the fix must not silently relax it.\n\n## Portability\n\nThe fix is in-process and platform-neutral. It is triggered by the *file's* shape (a `gitdir:` pointer), not by `os.name`, and not by any CI provider. It therefore holds on a developer's Windows checkout and in any CI system or none, satisfying `project.portability`.\n\n## Test strategy\n\nA regression test simulates the Windows-shaped marker on POSIX by making the copied `.git` pointer read-only before the rewrite, then asserts the copied store remains self-contained. This reproduces the structural mechanism — an in-place rewrite of a read-only `gitdir:` marker — without requiring a Windows host.\n\nThe test must be shown FAILING against the pre-fix code before the fix is applied.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `tests/_topology_template.py` — the guarded rewrite.\n- A regression test covering the read-only `gitdir:` pointer path.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The regression test reproduces the defect: it FAILS against pre-fix `_topology_template.py` with a permission error on the read-only `gitdir:` marker, and passes after the fix.\n- [ ] `_rewrite_embedded_paths()` restores the pointer file's original mode after writing, verified by asserting the mode before and after.\n- [ ] The guard keys on the `gitdir:` byte prefix of a `.git` file, not on `os.name` or any platform check.\n- [ ] Non-`.git` metadata files follow the unchanged write path, verified by an existing-behaviour test.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` passes.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass.\n- [ ] `make verify` shows no new failures beyond the known environmental set.\n- [ ] The Windows advisory sweep run after this lands no longer reports the `.tickets-tracker\\.git` `PermissionError` class. [non-codebase]\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- The MAX_PATH policy decision and the \"should the Windows sweep be a gate\" decision — both remain on `6798-606d` pending the user.\n- The other five cause classes in the sweep.\n- The seven test-only sites that make the same `.git`-is-a-directory assumption; they sit outside this defect and some may deliberately fabricate full `.git` directories.","id":"d724-6bb0-2674-42a0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["windows","portability","test-fixture"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Store template copy fails on read-only gitdir pointer"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789925769104079498,"uuid":"e3fa1afa-e790-4a42-b650-64f7a17205cf"}